# The Anchor's site blocks, as installed into the shared Caddyfile on the
# Hostinger VPS at /home/deploy/cs-tracker/Caddyfile.
#
# This is a fragment, not a standalone configuration, and no Caddy in this
# repository's compose stack reads it. The box runs one Caddy
# (cs-tracker-caddy-1) that owns ports 80 and 443 for the whole estate; the
# Anchor attaches to that Caddy's network under the aliases `anchor-app` and
# `anchor-umami`, which is how the reverse_proxy targets below resolve. Running
# a second binder of 80 or 443 on that box is what took cuatro.dev down.
#
# Installing it: back the shared Caddyfile up as Caddyfile.bak-1-21, append
# these blocks, run `caddy validate`, reload, then re-verify cs-tracker,
# tracker and library immediately. Restore the backup if any of the three
# regressed.
#
# All three hostnames must be DNS-only, Cloudflare proxy off, before these
# blocks are first loaded. Caddy issues over HTTP-01 on this box and a proxied
# record breaks the challenge, leaving the host with no certificate at all.
#
# The header set is the estate's, read off the live tracker.cuatro.dev block on
# 2026-08-17 and matched deliberately rather than improved on. Two headers were
# considered and left out: Strict-Transport-Security, because no host in the
# estate sends it today and adding it here would make this migration step carry
# a transport-policy decision it has no mandate for (AD-20), and `-Server`, for
# the same reason. Both are recorded as deferred work rather than dropped
# silently. X-Frame-Options is DENY, as on tracker; library uses SAMEORIGIN
# only because its EPUB reader frames its own content, and the Hub frames
# nothing.
#
# Indentation is tabs, which is what `caddy fmt` produces. Keep it that way so
# appending this fragment does not make the shared file report as unformatted.

cuatro.dev {
	header {
		X-Content-Type-Options "nosniff"
		X-Frame-Options "DENY"
		Referrer-Policy "strict-origin-when-cross-origin"
	}
	reverse_proxy anchor-app:3000
}

# The apex is canonical. www redirects and never serves a duplicate, so every
# Registry `live` value and every acceptance criterion naming the apex stays
# true. {uri} preserves path and query.
www.cuatro.dev {
	header {
		X-Content-Type-Options "nosniff"
		X-Frame-Options "DENY"
		Referrer-Policy "strict-origin-when-cross-origin"
	}
	redir https://cuatro.dev{uri} permanent
}

analytics.cuatro.dev {
	header {
		X-Content-Type-Options "nosniff"
		X-Frame-Options "DENY"
		Referrer-Policy "strict-origin-when-cross-origin"
	}
	reverse_proxy anchor-umami:3000
}
